FLAC input plugin
=================

Imported from FLAC 1.4.1 (https://github.com/xiph/flac, tag 1.4.1), the
last FLAC release that shipped its XMMS plugin; FLAC 1.4.2 removed it.
Files were copied verbatim from these locations in the FLAC tree:

  src/plugin_xmms/*                 ->  ./
  src/plugin_common/*               ->  plugin_common/
  include/share/*.h                 ->  share/
  include/share/grabbag/*.h         ->  share/grabbag/
  src/share/grabbag/alloc.c         ->  share/grabbag/
  src/share/grabbag/replaygain.c    ->  share/grabbag/
  src/share/replaygain_synthesis/*  ->  share/replaygain_synthesis/

Changes for the XMMS tree:

  * XMMS headers are included the way in-tree plugins do
    ("libxmms/...", "xmms/plugin.h"); <xmms/util.h> would otherwise
    pick up the XMMS program's internal util.h.
  * plugin.c uses snprintf() instead of FLAC's internal
    flac_snprintf().
  * http.c is gone: streams are fetched by the HTTP code the input
    plugins share, in Input/common, which also keeps the streaming
    settings. The Icecast 1 UDP title channel went with it.
  * The plugin reports its own version (1.4.1), not XMMS's VERSION.
  * share/grabbag/replaygain.c keeps only the functions the plugin
    uses (loading ReplayGain tags, computing the scale factor), so
    FLAC's replaygain_analysis library is not needed; the grabbag
    headers the plugin does not use are removed. The plugin is
licensed under the GNU GPL version 2 or later (COPYING.GPL); some
helpers under share/ are under Xiph.Org's BSD-like licence
(COPYING.Xiph), as stated in each file. It links against libFLAC.
